Specialty/Competency: IFS - Clients & Markets

Industry/Sector: Not Applicable

Time Type: Full time

Travel Requirements: Up to 20%

A career in National Special Functions, within Business Services, will provide you with the opportunity to support service, sector, and market leaders to deliver the unique PwC client experience to our clients. You'll play an important part in continuously innovating and improving Firm operations so that we can continue to provide the highest quality of services to our current and prospective clients. Our PwC Intelligence team is responsible for serving as a strategic business partner for an assigned customer to identify and pursue new opportunities, conduct market analysis, and prepare revenue projections. You'll also develop new service offerings and solutions, enhance existing delivery capabilities, and support the delivery of solutions on engagements.

To really stand out and make us fit for the future in a constantly changing world, each and every one of us at PwC needs to be a purpose-led and values-driven leader at every level. To help us achieve this we have the PwC Professional; our global leadership development framework. It gives us a single set of expectations across our lines, geographies and career paths, and provides transparency on the skills we need as individuals to be successful and progress in our careers, now and in the future.

Responsibilities

As a Senior Manager, you'll work as part of a team of problem solvers, helping to solve complex business issues from strategy to execution. PwC Professional skills and responsibilities for this management level include but are not limited to:
• Encourage everyone to have a voice and invite opinion from all, including quieter members of the team.
• Deal effectively with ambiguous and unstructured problems and situations.
• Initiate open and candid coaching conversations at all levels.
• Move easily between big picture thinking and managing relevant detail.
• Anticipate stakeholder needs, and develop and discuss potential solutions, even before the stakeholder realises they are required.
• Contribute technical knowledge in area of specialism.
• Contribute to an environment where people and technology thrive together to accomplish more than they could apart.
• Navigate the complexities of cross-border and/or diverse teams and engagements.
• Initiate and lead open conversations with teams, clients and stakeholders to build trust.
• Uphold the firm's code of ethics and business conduct.

Basic Qualifications

Job Requirements and Preferences:

Minimum Degree Required

Bachelor Degree

Minimum Years Of Experience

6 year(s)

Preferred Qualifications

Degree Preferred:

Master Degree

Preferred Fields Of Study

Computer and Information Science, Mathematics, Engineering, Economics, Statistics

Preferred Knowledge/Skills

Demonstrates intimate abilities and/or a proven record of success as a team leader:
• Owning thorough statistical knowledge with preference given to experience with time-series forecasting and machine learning;
• Having a thorough knowledge of software engineering industry-leading practices, including version control, Github, testing, and validation;
• Performing complex data analysis using tools such as Python (pandas, Anaconda python distribution);
• Demonstrating experience with API or rest service integrations, advanced SQL (common table expressions, use of temp tables, indexing), and other technical methods to extract and combine data from various sources;
• Displaying experience with SQL Server, as well as data transformation tools such as SSIS, Informatica, and DBT;
• Exhibiting experience working with financial data providers such as S&P Global, Refinitiv, Dealogic, or Audit Analytics;
• Being responsible for the creation and maintenance of data science pipelines with a focus on time series forecasting and model evaluation;
• Conducting quantitative and qualitative analyses of large and complex datasets;
• Building and managing ETL processes to transform data and schedule jobs;
• Working on multiple projects simultaneously;
• Revealing a conviction to high standards for data quality with a client-service focus;
• Taking ownership of developing relationships across the organization and serving as a data subject matter specialist (SMS);
• Laboring independently and with a team and able to efficiently communicate in written and verbal formats to both technical and non-technical audiences;
• Establishing relationships and work well across functions;
• Building, maintaining, and troubleshooting development and production environments;
• Cooperating with other areas of the firm to source data as needed;
• Possessing facilitation skills and the ability to coach/teach others;
• Demonstrating written and verbal communication skills, including problem/conflict resolution skills; and,
• Having direct engagement with functional leaders/staff and LOS leaders/staff.

Learn more about how we work: https://pwc.to/how-we-work

PwC does not intend to hire experienced or entry level job seekers who will need, now or in the future, PwC sponsorship through the H-1B lottery, except as set forth within the following policy: https://pwc.to/H-1B-Lottery-Policy.

All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment at PwC without regard to race; creed; color; religion; national origin; sex; age; disability; sexual orientation; gender identity or expression; genetic predisposition or carrier status; veteran, marital, or citizenship status; or any other status protected by law. PwC is proud to be an affirmative action and equal opportunity employer.

For positions based in San Francisco, consideration of qualified candidates with arrest and conviction records will be in a manner consistent with the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance.

Applications will be accepted until the position is filled or the posting is removed, unless otherwise set forth on the following webpage. Please visit this link for information about anticipated application deadlines: https://pwc.to/us-application-deadlines

For positions in California, Colorado, Hawaii, Nevada, New York State, or Washington State, or for opportunities that will report to a supervisor, office or other work site in New York State, please visit the following link for pay range information: https://pwc.to/payrange-v1-ifsseniormanager

Security Clearance Required: Top Secret with eligibility for Sensitive Compartmented Information.

Ignite is seeking a Geospatial Intelligence (GEOINT) Integrator / Data Scientist to support the development of analytic methodologies oriented toward enabling the statistical analysis, predictive modeling, and data visualization objectives of an intelligence community client.

The employee will be responsible for advising and managing projects that require working within the Department of Defense and U.S. Intelligence Community to perform research and analysis on U.S. sensor systems and adversary threat capabilities. The employee shall also provide technical expertise in the appropriate phenomenologies, mission processes, data sources, and analytic disciplines to support intelligence production efforts. This work will support the understanding of designated events by providing expertise in physics, optics, phenomenology, sensor design, temporal/spatial analytics, and event reconstruction. The employee will be required to identify and integrate finished intelligence from multiple sources and aggregate the information into a variety of data science models and visualization formulas.

Locations:
• Primary location is Springfield, Virginia.

Duties:
• Interact with analysts, mission partners and others on analytical functionality and exploitation and related support tools;
• The employee will interface with necessary internal and external agencies to facilitate collaboration, data, collection, product sharing, and integration of required intelligence.
• Support collection planning events, testing, and exercises, to include ground truth testing, development of testing and exercise standard operating procedures, and liaising with DoD program offices.
• Deliver a broad range of scientific analysis, technical, and exercise support in the emerging aerospace threats mission area.
• Provide systems engineering, data expertise, analysis, and integration support including the development of CONOPS/TTPs for operational systems and technical advice, primarily in the form of technical support, experiments, and systems engineering products.
• Perform data analytics and develop solutions to use U.S. operational sensor data from various sources and apply it against emerging aerospace threats.
• Support the assessment of new analytical tools and the necessary standards to facilitate compatibility and greater efficiencies across the tools sets utilized by imagery/geospatial analysts;
• Work with minimal guidance and be fully capable of meeting most analytic methodology services without direction;
• Collaborate to provide accurate technical information that contributes to synergized analysis that is better than the sum of the individual parts;
• Apply mathematical techniques to solve complex problems and develop quantitative based assessments;
• Apply scientifically based approaches to help solve complex intelligence problems and issues to include: statistical data analysis, knowledge discovery, and mathematical modeling;
• Provide database consultation, graphical data visualizations, and recommendations for quantitative data selection, intelligence collection & integration;
• Work rapidly in a high tempo, high stress environment that often requires multi-tasking.

Job Requirements

Education, Experience, & Licensing Requirements:
• Master’s Degree in a related field preferred;
• Attendance in a basic Intelligence Course is preferred;
• Previous experience as a GEOINT Analyst in a data driven/statistically driven environment or as a Data Scientist in support of an Intelligence Community mission;
• Previous intelligence integration experience a plus;
• Previous experience as an Operations Research/Systems Analyst (ORSA) a plus.

Required Skills:
• Familiarity with the US GEOINT enterprise in relation to aerospace threats and can work with the U.S. Intelligence Community, industry, and other government agencies to enable solutions;
• Proficiency with multi-sensor phenomenology ;
• Matlab, Python, Java, and C expertise to develop the user-facing tools, and understanding of data visualization capabilities;
• Experience in developing innovative design or system-related specifications and implementations, ensuring alignment with technical and business architectures;
• Experience with the use of enterprise architecture frameworks like DoD Architecture Framework (DoDAF);
• Ability to understand and assimilate intelligence threat analysis and technical aerospace-related data to produce coherently written analysis suitable for senior leadership;
• The ability to analyze complex problems in a clear and concise manner demonstrating attention to detail and a commitment to accuracy;
• Strong critical thinking and problem-solving skills with the ability to work independently or as part of a team with good customer engagement skills;
• Demonstrated strong collaboration and communication skills to effectively persuade, negotiate and bring consensus among differing opinions and views;
• Ability to apply knowledge of analytic tools to develop models, visualize data, and perform a range of analyses (e.g., systems analysis, comparative analysis).

Desired Skills:
• Knowledge of statistical analysis and visualization tools such as Tableau or similar tools;
• Familiarity with knowledge of GEOINT operations and sensors, which can be applied to satisfy key intelligence questions;
• Demonstrated relevant expertise in understanding of statistical/mathematical analysis in order to apply statistical/mathematical techniques to GEOINT;
• Demonstrated expertise in employing one or more of the following methodologies: statistical modeling; experimental design; research design; sampling; clustering; data reduction; confidence intervals; testing modeling, or predictive modeling in support of an intelligence mission;
• Demonstrated relevant expertise with analytic methodologies in support of intelligence production;
• Proficiency with orbital dynamics tools (e.g., OD++, STK, SOAP, Freeflyer);
• Demonstrated expertise with GIS and remote sensing tools such as: ArcGIS/ArcPro or Boundless Desktop GIS;
• Demonstrated proficiency with a programming language such as R, Python or similar.
